,[9.32,9.36,9.26,9.35,484500]],"about":{"what":"Entravision Communications Corporation (EVC). This chart runs from Jan 18, 2007 to May 25, 2007.","setup":"The stock rose about 40% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 6 weeks, peaking at $9.99 and pulling back 17% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Apr 9, 2007 it closed at $9.99, its first close above the base high of $10.00. Volume that day was 329K shares, 0.69x the prior 10-day average of 473K. It never committed. The best close afterward was $10.31, within 5% of the level, and the chart ends at $9.35.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakout that never resolved. Price chopped around the level without committing either way. Sitting it out, or getting out flat, was a fine read."}}